# chktex configuration for this paper. Run from this directory:
#
#     chktex -q main.tex
#
# Four warnings are suppressed, each because it has a 100% false-positive rate
# on this document -- checked entry by entry on 16 August 2026, not assumed:
#
#   3   "You should enclose the previous parenthesis with braces." Fires on
#       every \left( ... \right) pair in the algebra. 76 hits, all correct.
#   24  "Delete this space to maintain correct pagereferences." Fires on
#       \label{...} sitting on its own line, which is this file's convention.
#       23 hits.
#   36  "You should put a space in front of parenthesis." Fires on
#       Lemma~\ref{...}(i), which is the intended typography. 12 hits.
#   8   "Wrong length of dash may have been used." Fires on `--' between
#       letters. Every hit is a correct en-dash: Galbraith--Paterson--Smart,
#       Reed--Muller, Reed--Solomon, Berlekamp--Welch, Lang--Weil, and the
#       `Advances in Cryptology -- CRYPTO 20xx' proceedings titles in the
#       bibliography. 11 hits. Note this warning fires on `--' where a hyphen
#       might belong, not the reverse, so suppressing it cannot mask a missing
#       en-dash.
#
# Everything else stays on. As of 16 August 2026 the file is clean under this
# config, and `lacheck main.tex` is silent.

CmdLine
{
    -n3
    -n24
    -n36
    -n8
}
